"Greek", "meaning": "contrary to, beside", "meaning_zh": "\u30456 \u21453 \u12289 \u20559 \u38626 \u12289 \u22312 \u26049 " \}, \{ "root": "doxa", "origin": "Greek", "meaning": "opinion, belief", "meaning_zh": "\u35264 \u40670 \u12289 \u20449 \u24565 " \} ] \}, "mnemonic": \{ "root_memory": "PARA\u65288 \u30456 \u21453 \u65289 + DOXA\u65288 \u24120 \u35215 \u35264 \u40670 \u65289 \u8594  \u33287 \u22823 \u30526 \u24120 \u35672 \u30456 \u21453 \u65292 \u21371 \u38577 \u21547 \u30495 \u29702 \u30340 \u35498 \u27861 ", "story_en": "The speaker voiced an opinion PARA (contrary to) the public DOXA (belief), introducing a fascinating PARADOX.", "story_zh": "\u28436 \u35611 \u32773 \u25552 \u20986 \u20102 \u33287 \u20844 \u30526 \u12300 \u20449 \u24565 \u65288 DOXA\u65289 \u12301 \u12300 \u30456 \u21453 \u65288 PARA\u65289 \u12301 \u30340 \u35264 \u40670 \u65292 \u24341 \u20837 \u20102 \u19968 \u20491 \u36855 \u20154 \u30340 \u12300 \u24726 \u35542 \u65288 PARADOX\u65289 \u12301 \u12290 ", "emojis": ["\u9203 ", "\u55357 \u56580 ", "\u55358 \u56800 "] \}, "example": "It is a strange paradox that some of the world's richest countries contain pockets of extreme poverty.", "example_zh": "\u19990 \u30028 \u19978 \u19968 \u20123 \u26368 \u23500 \u26377 \u30340 \u22283 \u23478 \u20013 \u21371 \u23384 \u22312 \u33879 \u26997 \u24230 \u36007 \u22256 \u30340 \u35282 \u33853 \u65292 \u36889 \u26159 \u19968 \u20491 \u22855 \u30064 \u30340 \u30683 \u30462 \u29694 \u35937 \u65288 \u24726 \u35542 \u65289 \u12290 ", "collocations": [ "apparent paradox", "strange paradox", "economic paradox", "resolve a paradox", "central paradox" ], "synonyms": ["contradiction", "anomaly", "oxymoron", "enigma"], "near_synonyms": [ \{ "word": "contradiction", "difference": "contradiction implies a direct logical error where two statements cannot both be true; paradox describes something that 
