399 ", "\u55358 \u56784 ", "\u55357 \u56492 "] \}, "example": "The detective noted that while the suspect's story was plausible, it lacked physical evidence.", "example_zh": "\u20597 \u25506 \u25351 \u20986 \u65292 \u38614 \u28982 \u23244 \u30097 \u20154 \u30340 \u35498 \u36781 \u32893 \u36215 \u20358 \u21512 \u24773 \u21512 \u29702 \u65288 \u35498 \u24471 \u36890 \u65289 \u65292 \u20294 \u32570 \u20047 \u23526 \u39636 \u35657 \u25818 \u12290 ", "collocations": [ "plausible explanation", "perfectly plausible", "scarcely plausible", "plausible scenario", "highly plausible" ], "synonyms": ["credible", "believable", "feasible", "tenable"], "near_synonyms": [ \{ "word": "credible", "difference": "credible means something can be trusted because it is backed by authoritative evidence or a reliable witness; plausible only means it 
